	Confusion Matrix Analysis:
A confusion matrix is used to compute the following metrics:
•	True Positives (TP): Correctly predicted values for a specific class (diagonal elements).
•	False Negatives (FN): True values that were misclassified into another class (sum of rows excluding the diagonal element for that class).
•	False Positives (FP): Predicted values that belong to a different class (sum of columns excluding the diagonal element for that class).
•	True Negatives (TN): Correctly identified as not belonging to a specific class (everything except TP, FN, FP).
